the plot. **Fixed here:** (1) gensymb's `\\degree` was dropped by pandoc without a trace (\"17F\" for 17 °F) and `$\\deg$` stayed raw math; both are rewritten to `\\textdegree` before pandoc, restoring 23 degree signs in chapters 2, 3a, 3b and 3c. ComStock's guide uses neither macro, so its output is unchanged. (2) ResStock's decorative rule: all 28 reports open with cover art then the laboratory wordmark (four cover bitmaps and two wordmark bitmaps cover all 28, each one looked at), so it gets the OSTI-report rule and 56 bare image refs become omission comments. Sandbox rebuilt and validated after both. **Three shaping questions, decided by the owner 2026-11-10 (all as recommended):** (a) chapter files with more than one top-level heading: `3c_ResStockInputs` has seven H1s (Water Heating to Household Characteristics, all sections of the chapter that starts in 3a) and takes its title from the first, \"Water Heating\"; `2_ResStockStructureAndSampling` holds two chapters; section files cut on H2, so each extra H1 and its intro land at the tail of the previous section file. (b) `docs/FAQ.md` is 48 `<details><summary>` blocks of raw HTML, so no question is a heading. (c) the `ahs` / `AHS` citation key from R3.1. **What was done for each.** (a) Title only: a chapter document with several top-level headings is titled with all of them, in order (`3c` is now \"Water Heating, Appliances, Lighting, Plug Loads, Electric Vehicles, Electrical Panels, Household Characteristics\"; chapter 2 is \"ResStock Workflow, Input Structure and Sampling\"). Heading levels and the section files are unchanged, so each extra top-level heading and its intro still sit at the end of the previous section file; `sections.json` lists them with line ranges. ComStock's 19 chapters have one top-level heading each and are unaffected. (b) The markdown extractor unfolds `<details>` blocks: each `<summary>` becomes a heading one level below the heading it sits under (nested blocks one more each), the shared indentation of the body is removed so it is not read as a code block, and its simple HTML (`<p>`, `<a>`, `<ul>/<li>`, bold, italic) becomes markdown. The FAQ now has 48 question headings and no `<details>`, `<p>` or `<a>` tag left; one `<pre><code>` block is kept as HTML. The rule also applies to three ComStock pages at ComStock's next rebuild (`publications.md`, `utility_bills_emissions_known_issue.md`, `aws_athena_queries.md`; previewed, every block becomes a heading, code fences intact), a fourth change for that changelog entry. (c) A cited key with no exact match in the bibliography is respelled as the one key that equals it ignoring case; none or several, and it is left alone. The American Housing Survey citation now resolves and the build has no warnings. Worth reporting to the ResStock repo all the same. **End state:** full test suite passes; sandbox rebuild 62 documents, 0 warnings, validates; latex 0 dangling refs and character hygiene 0; pdf orphans unchanged at 2 tables and 15 figures, all for R4; ComStock still validates. | M |\n| R3.3 | Commit the first real build to `processed/resstock/…` with `--corpus-version resstock_amy2018_2025_release_1-v1-pre` or no version (the manifest's `corpus_version` only has to equal the tag at release time); `bsc map`, `bsc validate`. | `processed/resstock/**` | Validate green; `CORPUS_MAP.md` lists every document, the 32-measure routing table and the gap (measure 11, two notebooks). **Done 2026-11-11, branch `r3-first-build`.** Built with `--corpus-version resstock_amy2018_2025_release_1-v1-pre`, overlays on (there are none yet): 62 documents (7 guide chapters, 27 site pages, 28 measure PDFs), 3,772 chunks, 1,149 section files, 56 decorative image refs omitted, crosswalk 32 / 32 / 0, no warnings. 1,279 files committed under `processed/resstock/` (markdown and JSON; the 606 images are gitignored as ComStock's are). `bsc map` and `bsc validate` green for ResStock; ComStock still validates and its map regenerates identically apart from the timestamp. From this commit on, CI's validate loop checks ResStock too. Three things the map could not say were added so the done-when holds: (1) measure ids that are bare numbers sorted \"10\" before \"2\" in the crosswalk, the map's routing table and `index.json`; ids now sort with digit runs as numbers (ComStock's zero-padded ids keep their order). (2) A source can declare `not_converted` files in the registry, each with a reason; the manifest records them under `gaps.not_converted` and the map lists them under Known gaps. The two `.ipynb` how-to guides are declared (D4). (3) The registry can carry `notes` on the release, which the map lists under \"About this release\": that the AMY2012 dataset shares this documentation (D2), and which ref the guide text comes from and why it can differ from the published PDF (D1, the first open risk). Measure 11 is no longer a gap, so the map's only known gaps are the two notebooks. 8 new tests (`test_release_notes_and_gaps.py`). | S |\n",
